<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
        Slack's Compose lint rule discourages new CompositionLocals. We define
        exactly one — LocalNubecitaTokens — to expose the brand token bundle
        (spacing, elevation, motion). Allow it explicitly; any *other* new
        CompositionLocal in :designsystem still triggers the warning.
    -->
    <issue id="ComposeCompositionLocalUsage">
        <option name="allowed-composition-locals" value="LocalNubecitaTokens" />
    </issue>

    <!--
        MaterialTheme.spacing / .elevation / .typography / etc. are extension
        properties on MaterialTheme — the canonical Material 3 design-system
        token pattern (matches the M3 docs and every reference design system
        in the wild). MaterialTheme isn't @Stable, so the rule fires; the
        recomposition cost is negligible because the extension just reads
        from a CompositionLocal that returns a stable data class.
    -->
    <issue id="ComposeUnstableReceiver">
        <ignore path="src/main/kotlin/net/kikin/nubecita/designsystem/Tokens.kt" />
    </issue>

    <!--
        New in compose-lints 1.5.4. The rule guards against a slot whose
        INVOKING LOCATION moves under a condition: Compose treats the two
        positions as different, so the slot's internal state is dropped when
        it switches. That harm can't occur for the video slots here.

        The flagged parameters (PostCard's videoEmbedSlot / quotedVideoEmbedSlot
        and PostCardQuotedPost's quotedVideoEmbedSlot) are each used twice
        inside a `when` over a sealed embed type — invoked directly in the
        Video branch, forwarded down in the RecordWithMedia branch. Three
        reasons that is safe:

        1. The branches are mutually exclusive, and `PostUi.embed` is a `val`
           on an @Immutable model. A given post cannot transition from Video to
           RecordWithMedia, so the invoking location never moves for a post.
        2. PostCard renders inside keyed lazy lists, so two posts with
           different embed types never share a composition slot.
        3. The state the rule protects isn't in the composition anyway — the
           slot hosts the app-scoped single-player SharedVideoPlayer, which
           owns playback state outside Compose by design (:core:video).

        Scoped to the two files rather than disabled module-wide, so a genuine
        slot-reuse elsewhere in :designsystem still fails the build. The
        alternative — restructuring PostCard's embed dispatch so each slot is
        referenced once — is a real change to a core component with many
        committed baselines, and is not something a dependency bump should
        carry.
    -->
    <issue id="SlotReused">
        <ignore path="src/main/kotlin/net/kikin/nubecita/designsystem/component/PostCard.kt" />
        <ignore path="src/main/kotlin/net/kikin/nubecita/designsystem/component/PostCardQuotedPost.kt" />
    </issue>
</lint>
